1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,350
Good evening. King's Restaurant.

2
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:08,140
Good evening. I'm ringing about the job I understand you have vacant.

3
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:09,000
Oh yes.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,730
I'd like to find out a few more details, if I may.

5
00:00:11,730 --> 00:00:13,820
Yes, of course. Can I take your name?

6
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:15,710
It's Peter Chin.

7
00:00:15,710 --> 00:00:19,820
Okay Peter. Well, if you want to ask about the job

8
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:21,624
and then if we're both still interested,

9
00:00:21,624 --> 00:00:24,910
we could arrange for you to come for an interview.

10
00:00:24,910 --> 00:00:29,280
Great, thanks. I'm afraid I missed the advert for the job

11
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:31,000
but heard about it from a friend.

12
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:33,690
That's no problem at all. What would you like to know?

13
00:00:33,690 --> 00:00:37,920
Well, um, what sort of work is it - washing up?

14
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:40,070
It's answering the phone.

15
00:00:40,070 --> 00:00:42,530
Oh right, fine.

16
00:00:42,530 --> 00:00:44,940
And not waiting at table.

17
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:49,400
That'd be good. And how many nights a week would it be?

18
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:52,500
Well, we're really only busy at the weekend.

19
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:54,000
So two nights?

20
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,920
Three actually, so it would work out at twelve hours a week.

21
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:01,280
That'd be fine. It wouldn't interfere with my studies.

22
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:02,850
Are you at the university?

23
00:01:02,850 --> 00:01:04,900
Yes. First year Physics student.

24
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:06,030
Oh, right.

25
00:01:06,030 --> 00:01:11,430
Um, and because I'm not an EU national would I need a work permit?

26
00:01:11,430 --> 00:01:14,560
Yes you would. Just get your tutor to sign it.

27
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:16,080
That wouldn't be a problem

28
00:01:16,080 --> 00:01:21,050
if I were to get the job. Um, where exactly is the restaurant?

29
00:01:21,050 --> 00:01:27,000
Well, we have two branches - the one we're recruiting for is in Hillsdunne Road.

30
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,970
I don't know that. How do you spell it please?

31
00:01:30,970 --> 00:01:37,400
It's H. I-double L-S-D-U-double N-E Road.

32
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:42,250
Got that. Thanks. Is it near a bus stop?

33
00:01:42,250 --> 00:01:46,050
Yes. The nearest one would probably be just beside the Library.

34
00:01:46,050 --> 00:01:52,120
Oh yes, I know it. That'd be fine for me. And could I ask about the pay?

35
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:55,270
We're offering £4.45 an hour.

36
00:01:55,270 --> 00:02:00,800
That's very good. My last job was 3.95 an hour.

37
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:06,090
We feel it's pretty good and we also offer some good fringe benefits.

38
00:02:06,090 --> 00:02:06,850
Really?

39
00:02:06,850 --> 00:02:10,200
Well, we give you a free dinner, so you eat well.

40
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:12,660
Right, better than hostel food!

41
00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:17,910
We certainly hope so! And we also offer extra pay for working on national holidays.

42
00:02:17,910 --> 00:02:20,200
Oh, that's a really good perk, isn't it?

43
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:24,668
Yes, we think so. And then because of the difficulties of getting public transport,

44
00:02:24,668 --> 00:02:27,860
if you're working after 11 o'clock we drive you home.

45
00:02:27,860 --> 00:02:29,490
Oh, that's good to know.

46
00:02:29,490 --> 00:02:34,850
Well, we'd certainly be interested in inviting you for an interview, if you're still interested?

47
00:02:34,850 --> 00:02:40,870
Oh yes, certainly. Could I just also ask what qualities you're looking for?

48
00:02:40,870 --> 00:02:47,670
Well, for this particular job we want a clear voice, which you obviously do have!

49
00:02:47,670 --> 00:02:49,640
Thanks.

50
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:52,800
And you must be able to think quickly, you know.

51
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:54,400
Well, I hope I'd...

52
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:59,230
So, when could you come in for an interview? We're actually quite quiet tonight?

53
00:02:59,230 --> 00:03:01,720
Sorry, I couldn't come tonight

54
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:07,630
Or tomorrow, I'm afraid. Thursday's okay - that'd be 22nd of October.

55
00:03:07,630 --> 00:03:09,660
Fine, after 5 p. m.?

56
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:12,840
Yes, fine. Would 6 o'clock be okay?

57
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:17,220
Perfect. And could you bring along with the names of two referees?

58
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:18,870
Yes, that's fine, no problem.

59
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:21,200
Good, I look forward to seeing you.

60
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:24,520
Oh, by the way, who should I ask for?

61
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:28,320
Oh yes, of course, sorry. My name is Samira Manuja.

62
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:30,800
Can you spell that, please?

63
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:34,730
M-A-N-U-J-A.

64
00:03:34,730 --> 00:03:38,940
Okay, I've got that. Thanks very much.

65
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:40,940
Look forward to seeing you...
